        "original_id": "e09895b1-b1b4-57fe-a40f-c577189fafe4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rudolf Sieczyński, Stanley Kubrick, Arthur Schnitzler\n- Works: \"Vienna, City of My Dreams\", \"Eyes Wide Shut\", \"Traumnovelle\" (\"Dream Story\")\n- Places: Vienna, New York City\n\nFacts:\n- Rudolf Sieczyński composed and wrote the lyrics for the 1914 song \"Vienna, City of My Dreams\" (German: \"Wien, du Stadt meiner Träume\").\n- Arthur Schnitzler wrote the 1926 novella \"Traumnovelle\" (\"Dream Story\").\n- Stanley Kubrick's film \"Eyes Wide Shut\" is based on Arthur Schnitzler's 1926 novella \"Traumnovelle\" and transfers the story from early 20th-century Vienna to 1990s New York City.\n- The song \"Vienna, City of My Dreams\" was featured in the soundtrack of Stanley Kubrick's film \"Eyes Wide Shut\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
